    "narrative_direction": "Public sentiment is highly polarized and volatile. The narrative will likely shift from a debate on the necessity of infrastructure upgrades to a crisis of governance due to the procurement scandal involving Brightline Consulting. The union's threat of a strike adds immediate operational risk, while the City Council's vote on July 15th acts as a focal point for all stakeholders. If the plan passes without job guarantees, the narrative will turn towards civil disobedience and labor unrest; if it fails, it will focus on fiscal irresponsibility and the cost of the scandal.",
